[2026-03-14T20:09:49.949Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UniR59Aufv94K78doqWSva","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NvavTrL9r3ZEru6sFLNWB7","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/docs/tests.md","offset":200,"limit":100},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4680,"cache_read_input_tokens":39356,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4680,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0114QLLRUEx1moAjra4ugLk7","session_id":"c9a6ccec-d137-4f6f-8279-aaabb9d3d1bc","uuid":"91927dc9-e96a-4737-8a33-d5aee9d709a6"}
[2026-03-14T20:09:49.963Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NvavTrL9r3ZEru6sFLNWB7","type":"tool_result","content":"   200→- **Expected:** The property card displays the main image (lowest display_order) at the top of the card with rounded top corners. If no image exists, a placeholder image is shown.\n   201→\n   202→#### Test: Clicking a property card navigates to property detail page\n   203→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property with id \"abc-123\" is displayed.\n   204→- **Action:** User clicks on the property card (not the favorite button).\n   205→- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page).\n   206→\n   207→#### Test: Property card displays property type badge\n   208→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of different types exist.\n   209→- **Expected:** Each property card shows a badge/label indicating the property type (e.g., \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\"). The badge is visually distinct (e.g., small colored label overlaying or near the image).\n   210→\n   211→#### Test: Property card displays average rating with review count\n   212→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property has an average rating of 4.2 from 8 reviews.\n   213→- **Expected:** The card shows a star icon with \"4.2\" and \"(8 reviews)\" or \"(8)\" next to it. If the property has no reviews, the rating section shows \"New\" or is not displayed.\n   214→\n   215→### Component: FavoriteButton\n   216→\n   217→#### Test: Favorite button shows outline heart when property is not favorited\n   218→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. The property is not in the user's favorites.\n   219→- **Expected:** The property card displays a heart icon with an outline (unfilled) style in the top-right corner of the card image.\n   220→\n   221→#### Test: Clicking favorite button on unfavorited property adds it to favorites\n   222→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. A property is not in their favorites.\n   223→- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on the property card.\n   224→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/favorites` with the property ID. The heart icon changes to a filled/solid red heart. The property is now in the user's favorites list.\n   225→\n   226→#### Test: Clicking favorite button on favorited property removes it from favorites\n   227→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. A property is already in their favorites (heart is filled/red).\n   228→- **Action:** User clicks the filled heart icon on the property card.\n   229→- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/favorites/:propertyId`. The heart icon changes back to an outline (unfilled) style. The property is removed from the user's favorites.\n   230→\n   231→#### Test: Favorite button does not navigate to property detail page\n   232→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page.\n   233→- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on a property card.\n   234→- **Expected:** The favorite is toggled but the user remains on the home page. The click does not propagate to the card's navigation handler.\n   235→\n   236→#### Test: Favorite button is not shown when user is not logged in\n   237→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in and is on the home page.\n   238→- **Expected:** Property cards do not display the heart/favorite icon. Alternatively, clicking the heart redirects the user to the login page.\n   239→\n   240→#### Test: Favorite button reflects correct state on page load\n   241→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has previously favorited two properties. User navigates to the home page.\n   242→- **Expected:** The app calls `GET /api/favorites` to fetch the user's favorites. The two favorited properties show filled/red hearts. All other properties show outline hearts.\n   243→\n   244→#### Test: Favorite button is functional on repeated use\n   245→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page with a property that is not favorited.\n   246→- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon (favorites it), then clicks it again (unfavorites it), then clicks it a third time (favorites it again).\n   247→- **Expected:** Each click correctly toggles the heart appearance and makes the appropriate API call. The final state is favorited (filled heart).\n   248→\n   249→### Component: FiltersPanel\n   250→\n   251→#### Test: Filters panel is hidden by default with a visible toggle button\n   252→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n   253→- **Expected:** The filters panel is collapsed/hidden. A \"Filters\" button (with a filter icon) is visible that the user can click to open the panel.\n   254→\n   255→#### Test: Clicking the Filters button opens the filters panel\n   256→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel hidden.\n   257→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Filters\" button.\n   258→- **Expected:** The filters panel opens/expands, revealing all filter controls: a price range slider, bedrooms minimum selector, beds minimum selector, bathrooms minimum selector, and amenity checkboxes grouped by category.\n   259→\n   260→#### Test: Clicking the Filters button again closes the filters panel\n   261→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   262→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Filters\" button again.\n   263→- **Expected:** The filters panel collapses/hides. The property grid remains showing the previously applied filters.\n   264→\n   265→#### Test: Price range slider filters properties by price per night\n   266→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with prices $50, $100, $200, and $500 per night.\n   267→- **Action:** User adjusts the price range slider to a minimum of $75 and a maximum of $250.\n   268→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with price_per_night between $75 and $250 (i.e., $100 and $200 properties). The slider visually reflects the selected range with labels showing the min and max values.\n   269→\n   270→#### Test: Bedrooms minimum filter works correctly\n   271→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with 1, 2, 3, and 5 bedrooms.\n   272→- **Action:** User sets the bedrooms minimum selector to 3.\n   273→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 3 or more bedrooms.\n   274→\n   275→#### Test: Beds minimum filter works correctly\n   276→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with varying bed counts.\n   277→- **Action:** User sets the beds minimum selector to 2.\n   278→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 2 or more beds.\n   279→\n   280→#### Test: Bathrooms minimum filter works correctly\n   281→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with 1, 2, and 3 bathrooms.\n   282→- **Action:** User sets the bathrooms minimum selector to 2.\n   283→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 2 or more bathrooms.\n   284→\n   285→#### Test: Amenity checkboxes filter properties by selected amenities\n   286→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Amenities include \"WiFi\", \"Pool\", \"Kitchen\", \"Parking\". Properties have varying amenities.\n   287→- **Action:** User checks the \"WiFi\" and \"Pool\" amenity checkboxes.\n   288→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that have both WiFi AND Pool amenities. The checked amenities remain visually checked.\n   289→\n   290→#### Test: Amenity checkboxes are grouped by category\n   291→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   292→- **Expected:** Amenity checkboxes are organized into groups labeled by category: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each group contains the relevant amenities.\n   293→\n   294→#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n   295→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   296→- **Action:** User sets price range to $100–$300, bedrooms minimum to 2, and checks the \"WiFi\" amenity.\n   297→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties that satisfy ALL three conditions: price between $100–$300, at least 2 bedrooms, and has WiFi amenity.\n   298→\n   299→#### Test: Filters combine with search bar and category filter"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0114QLLRUEx1moAjra4ugLk7","session_id":"c9a6ccec-d137-4f6f-8279-aaabb9d3d1bc","uuid":"5d7fde5b-56bb-41a0-8276-1c7a398bb713"}
